<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n56415" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεκᾰφηώς</span></b> , 
			Ep.
		
		pf.
		part. with no pres. in use, <i><span class="en">
			Hom.
		</span></i> only in phrase <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεκαφηότα θυμόν</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>breathing forth</i> one's
			life, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				5.698
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				5.468
			</span></i>: in later Poets intr., <i>worn out, fordone</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεκαφηότα γυῖα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Opp.
					<u>C.</u>
					4.206
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. γυῖα κεραυνῷ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nonn.
					<u>D.</u>
					2.539
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δέμας κ. λιμῷ</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				26.108
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δίψῃ κεκαφηότας</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				29.299
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνδρα . . κεκαφηότα
			δηϊοτῆτι</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				46.93
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεκαφηότι θυμῷ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Opp.
					<u>H.</u>
					3.572
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. ταρσῷ</span>”
				<i>weary,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					AP
					9.653
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Agath.
			</span></i>). (Cogn. with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καπύω,
			κάπτω</span>: <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> has <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κέκηφε:</span></b> 
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέθνηκεν</span>.)</div>
